   Home Assistant integration as published in the official repository), free of
   charge, including on websites, forums and SD-card bundles, as long as:
   a) the files are complete and unmodified, and include this license;
   b) you do not charge for them, sell them or include them in a paid product or
      service;
   c) you credit "NX Control by Daniel Alonso" and link to the official page:
      https://github.com/danialonso/nx-control

3. What is not allowed
   Unless the author gives written permission, you may not:
   a) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of NX Control, or share
      modified versions;
   b) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the console software, except to
      the extent permitted by applicable law;
   c) sell, rent, lend or sublicense NX Control, or use it as part of a commercial
      product or service;
   d) remove or change copyright notices, this license or the credits;
   e) use the name "NX Control" or its logo for other software, or in a way that
      suggests endorsement.

4. Third-party components
   NX Control includes third-party open-source components, each under its own
